 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The chronological structure in journalistic language",
     "texto": [
      "Short news items (**Kurznachrichten**) usually begin by reporting the main event in the **Präteritum** (the typical tense of German written media) or in the **Perfekt**.",
      "To detail the causes, background or events that triggered the situation, journalists systematically use the **Plusquamperfekt**:",
      "**Die Feuerwehr löschte den Brand im Stadtzentrum. Zuvor hatten Anwohner dichten Rauch bemerkt** (The fire brigade put out the fire in the city centre. Beforehand, residents had noticed thick smoke).",
      "Connectors such as **nachdem**, **zuvor** (beforehand) and **davor** (before that) help guide the reader along the timeline without confusion."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Chronological connector",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Function",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
